1.1.f - UNRELEASED
Fixed - Blackouts could leave the player in hidden systems deep in the abyss
Fixed - Drink production no longer makes Light Industry demand extra organics
Fixed - Crash after saving when other mods read markets of former colonies (reported by DeCEll-1)

1.1.e

General
Fixed - Daily stuttering in large fleets, especially when other mods checked cargo through skills or hullmods
Fixed - Small fleets consumed more alcohol than predicted by tooltips and supply warnings
Fixed - LunaLib settings failed to apply immediately after loading a second save in the same session

Drink effects
Fixed - Absynth's OP correction removed equipment from ships that had not been refitted under its effects, even in fleets that had never consumed Absynth
Fixed - Drink effects and Absynth's OP correction could affect matching modules on other ships of the same type until the game was restarted
Fixed - Sweet Freedom increased market tariffs instead of reducing them
Fixed - Sweet Freedom modified carrier damage against fighters instead of damage taken by the carrier's fighters, both while drinking and during withdrawal
Fixed - Reapers Blood allowed the zero-flux speed boost above its intended 30% flux limit
Fixed - Reapers Blood failed to make ships without officers aggressive while drinking and cautious during withdrawal
Fixed - Stout continued to regenerate armor during withdrawal
Fixed - Tears of Ludd applied its officer XP modifier one battle late and skipped the first battle after loading a save
Fixed - Loading a save during withdrawal disabled Sweet Freedom's tariff penalty and Tears of Ludd's officer XP penalty until drinking resumed

Blackouts
Fixed - Blackouts could strand the player in pulsar or black hole systems, or systems with no hyperspace access
Fixed - Blackouts could crash the game in starless systems or near planets and jump points without orbits
Fixed - The fleet separated by a blackout could rejoin the player from another star system
Fixed - The final blackout message did not appear
Fixed - Blackout calculations included 31 days of drinking history instead of 30

Markets
Fixed - Drink supply and demand remained after a market changed ownership, lost Light Industry or stopped receiving the player's drink exports
Fixed - Light Industry ignored the drinks required for production

Codex and tooltips
Fixed - Opening drink or drink hullmod entries from the main-menu Codex could crash the game
Adjusted - Codex hullmod entries show drink effects at full strength, with links between drinks, hullmods and recipes
Fixed - Prometheus Gift's withdrawal tooltip described a burn reduction as a negative number
Fixed - Hangover Cure's tooltip rounded the default 1.5x multiplier to 2x

Installation
Adjusted - The downloaded mod folder is now named Substance.Abuse, without a version number
Note - Delete the old Substance.Abuse1.1.d folder before installing

1.1.d
Added - Icon
Adjusted - Moved all settings to LunaLib
Fixed - Rare crash with certain industries
Fixed - Sweet Freedom now correctly reduces sensor profile instead of increasing it
Fixed - Sweet Freedom now properly reduces market Tariffs instead of increasing them

1.1.c
Adjusted - Brewery industry type: Industrial -> Rural
Adjusted - Economic value of alcohol halved
Adjusted - All Alcohol prices increased by ~1.66x
Adjusted - Consumption is now less than half of what it used to be (1 / month -> 0.4 / month)
Adjusted - Cargo space per unit 0.5 -> 1.0
Result: Carrying around 200 units now takes 200 space, but it lasts you around 2.5x as long. Stocking up is more expensive.

1.1.b
Adjusted - Compatibility patch for 0.97a

1.1.a
Adjusted - Compatibility patch for 0.96a

